# The build context. The stages copy only pyproject.toml, uv.lock, server.py,
# pkg/, lib/ and app/, so most of this is belt-and-braces — but the whole
# context is uploaded to the daemon before any COPY runs, and every file in it
# is a file that can bust the cache. Keeping it tight keeps `docker build` fast.
#
# Most important: .env must never enter the context. A secret is readable in an
# intermediate layer forever, even when the runtime stage copies nothing but
# the venv and the source tree.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log

# Resolved in the builder from uv.lock. A host venv is also the wrong platform
# (Windows Scripts/, macOS dylibs) and would be copied over a good one.
.venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache

.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.idea
.vscode
.claude
.mcp.json

# Dev aids — mock_core, mint_jwt, publish_test, check_mongo. Gitignored, never
# part of a build, and they would look like production entry points in an image.
play/

docs
*.md
*.png

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose-test.yml
